e_ids":[],"id":"step.common_distribution","kind":"claim","label":"One distribution for both errors","locator":"Proof of Theorem 4.1, p. 9","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"Both estimates use $\\mathscr D_{Q;M,M}$ with $Q=L\\prod_{p\\in P}p^{\\lfloor\\log_pH\\rfloor}$, $G=\\lfloor H/\\max P\\rfloor$, $M=\\lfloor2^{G/2}\\rfloor$. Then $\\mathscr D_{Q;M,M}(\\Delta_{2,E}/\\rho)<\\frac18$ and $\\mathscr D_{Q;M,M}S_J\\le(1+4Q/M)K_J<\\frac18$, so $\\mathscr D_{Q;M,M}(\\Delta_{2,E}/\\rho+S_J)<\\frac14$. This step uses only the linearity of the mean, and requires no independence between the two errors.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/step.common_distribution","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/short.res-mixed-supports","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22short.res-mixed-supports%22%2C%22step.common_distribution%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22short.res-mixed-supports%22%2C%22step.common_distribution%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/step.common_distribution"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/step.common_distribution","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22step.common_distribution%22%2C%22step.combined_bound%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22step.common_distribution%22%2C%22step.combined_bound%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256